                        "glosses": [
                            "Failure to notice; failure to be aware of; lack of apprehension."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbc15364-0294-4a30-9c46-b092800f6437",
                                "sense_id": "f0f4abe4-1123-345a-8f38-570a95c72a7c",
                                "text": "These, like the over-largely lettered signs and placards of the street, escape observation by dint of being excessively obvious; and here the physical oversight is precisely analogous with the moral inapprehension by which the intellect suffers to pass unnoticed those considerations which are too obtrusively and too palpably self-evident."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4c1261d-1119-42e2-8958-0628f234f9e5",
                                "sense_id": "f0f4abe4-1123-345a-8f38-570a95c72a7c",
                                "text": "He paled a little, and sucked his lip, his eyes wandering to the girl, who stood in stolid inapprehension of what was being said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3a85f1a-9fa9-4a92-be22-09a9bdce31d7",
                                "sense_id": "f0f4abe4-1123-345a-8f38-570a95c72a7c",
                                "text": "Camile is naturally disgusted with Paul but he doesn't seem to apprehend her reason—it is this inapprehension of the obvious which creates the tension."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
